# Line-ending policy for the generated files this repo commits on purpose.
#
# The plugin sample package is a ZIP produced by the MARKET repository's
# packaging script and copied here as the built-in offline source. Git's
# core.autocrlf rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout, and it does not know
# that a .zip is binary: with autocrlf on, the archived bytes were rewritten on
# the way into the object store, so the committed package no longer matched the
# sha256 its own catalogue publishes and the built-in source failed its own
# integrity check on a fresh clone.
#
# Marking archives binary (plus `-text` for the plugin sources that are copied
# into them) keeps the bytes that the digest was computed over.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary

# The embedded voice clips are already-compressed audio: same reasoning.
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary

# Plugin front-end sources and the packaged manifest. `-text` keeps them exactly
# as authored, so a re-packaged archive is byte-identical to the one committed
# here and the published hash stays valid.
*.html text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Windows scripts are consumed by PowerShell, which accepts LF, but keeping them
# LF avoids spurious diffs when the toolchain is the Linux side.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
